title: ZFS ARC cache usage
agents: linux
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution:
description:
 Monitors the ZFS Adaptive Replacement Cache (ARC) on a Linux host running
 OpenZFS. The plugin reads {/proc/spl/kstat/zfs/arcstats} and reports:

 - ARC size as a percentage of its configured maximum ({c_max}).
 - ARC size as a percentage of total system RAM.
 - The cache hit ratio ({hits} / ({hits} + {misses})).
 - The {memory_throttle_count} counter (nonzero indicates the kernel throttled
   ARC growth due to memory pressure).

 The check goes WARN if the ARC exceeds 90% of {c_max}, if it uses more than
 40% of total RAM, if the hit ratio drops below 85%, or if any memory
 throttling has occurred. It goes CRIT if RAM usage exceeds 60% or the hit
 ratio drops below 75%.

 The output also includes a heuristic recommendation (e.g. reduce or increase
 {zfs_arc_max}) based on the observed sizing and hit ratio, intended as a
 starting point for manual tuning — it is not applied automatically.

 This is implemented as a Checkmk **local check**
 ({agents/custom/zfs_arc/lib/local/zfs_arc.sh}), deployed manually to
 {$MK_LOCALDIR} (or {/usr/lib/check_mk_agent/local/}) on the monitored host. A
 companion plugin
 ({agents/custom/zfs_arc/lib/plugins/zfs_arc_cache}) emits the raw
 {arcstats} kstat values as a separate {<<<zfs_arc_cache>>>} section for
 anyone who wants to build additional checks against the raw counters; no
 check plugin in this package currently consumes that section.

 On hosts without ZFS (missing {/proc/spl/kstat/zfs/arcstats}) the local
 check reports UNKNOWN and does nothing else.

item:
 None. The check produces a single service {ZFS ARC}.

discovery:
 None — the local check output IS the service; no separate discovery step.
